<title>USA: Dauphin chairman to retire after merger.</title>
<headline>Dauphin chairman to retire after merger.</headline>
<dateline>HARRISBURG, Pa. 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dauphin Deposit Corp said on Monday that its chairman and chief executive, Christopher Jennings, will retire on July 8 when Dauphin is acquired by Allied Irish Banks Plc.</p>
<p>Jennings will serve as a member of the board of First Maryland Bancorp, an Allied Irish subsidiary into which Dauphin is to be merged, the company said in a news release.</p>
</text>
